---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Mohamed Hafez"
  description="Plain-language privacy details for Mohamed Hafez’s portfolio, including aggregate traffic measurement and the planned first-party event policy."
  roleId="aiml"
>
  <header class="longform-hero shell-container">
    <p class="utility-label">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Useful measurement without visitor profiles</h1>
    <p class="longform-hero__summary">
      This portfolio is designed to understand which pages and features are
      useful without building visitor profiles or storing chat content.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="privacy-record shell-container">
    <section aria-labelledby="traffic-measurement-title">
      <h2 id="traffic-measurement-title">Aggregate traffic measurement</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Web Analytics is the launch measurement service for page
        traffic and Core Web Vitals once I enable it for the production
        hostname. It is separate from the first-party custom-event system
        described below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="custom-events-title">
      <h2 id="custom-events-title">Future first-party custom events</h2>
      <p>
        A later analytics phase will add a first-party <code>/api/events</code>
        endpoint for normalized actions such as lens selection, case-study opening,
        résumé download, contact/profile clicks, and chat outcomes. That custom-event
        collection is not active in the current foundation.
      </p>
      <p>
        When enabled, permitted fields will be limited to route, active
        professional focus, target or project ID, question category, outcome,
        public source IDs, a coarse latency bucket, AI model ID, and a random
        session ID that is hashed on the server. It will not collect names,
        email addresses, phone numbers, exact IP addresses, full user agents,
        fingerprints, or cross-site identifiers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="chat-privacy-title">
      <h2 id="chat-privacy-title">Chat content</h2>
      <p>
        The design does not store raw chat questions or answers in analytics.
        Conversation history will stay in browser session storage only for the
        active session and will not be written to a permanent portfolio
        transcript.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="retention-title">
      <h2 id="retention-title">Retention after custom analytics launches</h2>
      <p>
        Once first-party custom events are enabled, raw anonymous-session events
        will expire after 30 days and daily aggregate counts will expire after
        180 days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-controls-title">
      <h2 id="privacy-controls-title">Privacy controls</h2>
      <p>
        The future custom-event client will honor Global Privacy Control and Do
        Not Track by disabling collection. It will also provide a local opt-out
        that stores only the opt-out choice, never a persistent visitor
        identifier.
      </p>
      <div
        class="analytics-opt-out-placeholder"
        data-analytics-opt-out-mount
        aria-live="polite"
      >
        <p>
          Custom event analytics is not active yet. This clearly marked hook
          will become the working local opt-out control in the analytics phase.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
